      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update python-3.12 to 3.12.13-r2 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-3644: the fix for CVE-2026-0672 in http.cookies was incomplete: Morsel.update(), the |= operator and unpickling still accepted control characters, and BaseCookie.js_output() lacked the output validation of BaseCookie.output(). Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/145599 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/3974092b037f9a3b000fb15b48ea61ce3b25d330), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/H6CADMBCDRFGWCMOXWUIHFJNV43GABJ7/ and https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-3644. Checked Lib/http/cookies.py for all four parts of the fix (the control-character checks in Morsel.update(), Morsel.__setstate__() and js_output(), and the new Morsel.__ior__()) in the python-3.12 package of every build published in the DHI Alpine 3.23 repository, 3.12.12-r0 to 3.12.16-r4, x86_64 and aarch64; both architectures agree. Builds before 3.12.13-r2 lack the fix; 3.12.13-r2 and every later build have it (3.12.12-r0 has none of the four parts; 3.12.13-r0 and 3.12.13-r1 ship the upstream 3.12.13 file, which also has none of the four parts; from 3.12.13-r2 on the file is identical to the upstream 3.12.14 file). The range ends at 3.12.13-r2."
    },
