      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update python-3.14 to 3.14.4-r1 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-3644: The fix for CVE-2026-0672 in http.cookies was incomplete: Morsel.update(), the |= operator and unpickling still accepted control characters, and BaseCookie.js_output() lacked the output validation of BaseCookie.output(). Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/145599 (3.14 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/62ceb396fcbe69da1ded3702de586f4072b590dd), first released in CPython 3.14.4; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/H6CADMBCDRFGWCMOXWUIHFJNV43GABJ7/; https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-3644. Compared Lib/http/cookies.py in every published build, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package on x86_64 and aarch64 with the files in the upstream CPython 3.14 releases. 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.3-r1 lack the fix; 3.14.4-r1 is the first published build that has it and is built from the upstream 3.14.4 release, and every later build carries it."
    },
