      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-3644: the fix for CVE-2026-0672 in http.cookies was incomplete: Morsel.update(), the |= operator and unpickling still accepted control characters, and BaseCookie.js_output() lacked the output validation of BaseCookie.output(). Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/145599 (3.12 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/3974092b037f9a3b000fb15b48ea61ce3b25d330), first released in CPython 3.12.14; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/H6CADMBCDRFGWCMOXWUIHFJNV43GABJ7/ and https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-3644. Checked Lib/http/cookies.py for all four parts of the fix (the control-character checks in Morsel.update(), Morsel.__setstate__() and js_output(), and the new Morsel.__ior__()) in the standard library shipped by the DHI Debian 13 python-3.12 packages (libpython-3.12-stdlib and libpython-3.12-minimal) in every build published in the DHI Debian repository, 3.12.13-0 to 3.12.16-8, amd64 and arm64; both architectures agree. Every published build has the fix (3.12.13-0 to 3.12.16-4 ship a file identical to the upstream 3.12.14 file; from 3.12.16-5 it also carries a separate change to js_output() and keeps all four parts), so the range ends at 3.12.13-0, the lowest published build."
